    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 462,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 375,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62791,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 142,
        "headingId": 375,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Peritoneum</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-19T15:13:46"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 463,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 376,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62792,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 142,
        "headingId": 376,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Most patients present with abdominal pain or distension, although in rare cases patients can present with lymphadenopathy {15316322; 15577686} or be asymptomatic {26076164}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-19T15:13:46"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 464,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 377,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62793,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 142,
        "headingId": 377,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Patient age ranges from 27 to 82&nbsp;years (median: 52&nbsp;years) {21397305}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-19T15:13:46"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 465,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 378,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62794,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 142,
        "headingId": 378,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-19T15:13:46"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 466,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 379,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62795,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 142,
        "headingId": 379,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Peritoneal LGSC can occur de novo or after the diagnosis of serous borderline tumour. The MAPK pathway appears to play an important role in the pathogenesis of this tumour {27141071}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-19T15:13:46"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 473,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 386,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62796,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 142,
        "headingId": 386,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>LGSC typically occurs as multiple nodules of variable size involving the peritoneum or omentum; however, rare cases are not associated with a distinct gross abnormality but are gritty or firm on tissue palpation or sectioning.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-19T15:13:46"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 467,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 380,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62797,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 142,
        "headingId": 380,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>LGSC shows neoplastic cells that are relatively uniform, with mild to moderate cytological atypia and a low mitotic count {15087669}. A variety of architectural patterns can be seen, including papillary, micropapillary, cribriform, solid, glandular, and nested patterns, as well as single cells. Extracytoplasmic or intracytoplasmic mucin, as well as a variable number of psammoma bodies, can be seen. Invasion into underlying tissues such as omentum, pelvic tissue, or abdominal/pelvic organs is present. There is no involvement of the ovaries {21397305}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-19T15:13:46"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 468,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 381,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62798,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 142,
        "headingId": 381,
        "headingText": "<p>Cytology samples show variable cellularity, large 3D papillary groups, and a variable number of single cells, as well as variable pleomorphism, N:C&nbsp;ratio, nuclear size, chromatin pattern, and psammoma bodies. Mitoses are rare {23858317}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-19T16:02:21"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 469,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 382,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62799,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 142,
        "headingId": 382,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-19T15:13:46"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 472,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 385,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62800,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 142,
        "headingId": 385,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> an invasive epithelial proliferation in the form of papillary/glandular structures; nests or single cells with mild to moderate cytological atypia; low mitotic count; gross or microscopic involvement of the ovaries excludes this diagnosis.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-19T15:13:46"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 470,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 383,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62801,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 142,
        "headingId": 383,
        "headingText": "<p>LGSC is staged according to the Union for International Cancer Control (UICC) TNM classification (see <em>TNM staging of ovarian, fallopian tube, and primary peritoneal carcinoma</em>&nbsp;[[Brierley JD, Gospodarowicz MK, Wittekind C, editors. TNM classification of malignant tumours. 8th ed. Oxford (UK): Wiley-Blackwell; 2017.]]) and the FIGO staging system.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-07-15T11:45:05"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 471,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 384,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 62802,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 142,
        "headingId": 384,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>A reported 72% of patients have persistent disease or progressive disease after the completion of primary treatment, despite an optimal cytoreduction rate of 75%. Like its ovarian counterpart, peritoneal LGSC shows a low response rate to conventional platinum-based chemotherapy {21397305}. The presence of <em>KRAS</em> mutations in peritoneal serous borderline tumour and LGSC also appears to be an adverse prognostic factor {29027536}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-05-19T15:13:46"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]